+### Failure forensics
+
+Every connector failure writes a capture: full-page screenshot, page HTML, final
+URL and title, under `CONNECTOR_FORENSICS_DIR` (`/app/forensics`, its own volume;
+newest 50 kept). A summary also goes into `SyncLog.metadata.forensics` and the
+log stream, so the URL and error are reachable without shell access to the
+container. Credentials the connector holds are stripped from the HTML first.
+`CONNECTOR_FORENSICS=off` disables it.
+
+The final URL is the field to read first: a redirect back to `/login` means the
+session died, which is indistinguishable from a missing selector at the call
+site.
+
+`ConnectorService` captures inside the `catch`, deliberately **before** the
+`finally` that closes the browser. Move the call after `close()` and there is no
+page left to photograph.
+
